# Continuation prompts

Prompts are operational instructions, not theorem sources. Always read
[`../STATE.md`](../STATE.md) and the selected target route map first.
Level I remains open; prompt filenames and detail do not establish theorem status.

## Current prompts

### Target A

[`erdos_problem_99_TARGET_A_CURRENT_CONTINUATION_PROMPT.md`](erdos_problem_99_TARGET_A_CURRENT_CONTINUATION_PROMPT.md)
is the active Target A prompt. It follows the canonical chain through Section 177.
Section 174's basis-closed shield charge is a historical intermediate; the preferred
locked endpoint is Section 175's interior-tube right-deficiency inequality. Sections
176–177 add zero-slack source and edge-lens/coarse-Hall refinements, but the required
conversion to Schur deficiency or a strict competitor remains open. The prompt's state
marker is checked against the current manifest.

### Target C

[`erdos_problem_99_TARGET_C_CURRENT_CONTINUATION_PROMPT.md`](erdos_problem_99_TARGET_C_CURRENT_CONTINUATION_PROMPT.md)
is the active Target C prompt. C-I is closed. The prompt starts C-II after the
strict-negative transfer theorem, Woodall diameter-topology classification, and
universal-common-contact-bridge exclusion. C-II remains open: its current full-core
branch needs a source-realized face-coupled finite move or discrete replacement, while
the separate macroscopic-container branch still lacks a packet-capacity or moved-core
strict-diameter closure. Audit.230's quarter-fold population count alone supplies
neither endpoint.

### Whole problem

[`erdos_problem_99_GPT6_ASTRA_FULL_SOLUTION_PROMPT.md`](erdos_problem_99_GPT6_ASTRA_FULL_SOLUTION_PROMPT.md)
is the current whole-problem launch prompt. Despite its historical model name, its
mathematical bootstrap is model-independent: it reads the state lock first and chooses
among the current A/B/C endpoints. Its state marker is checked against the current
manifest, and the Target C section follows the current full-core/macroscopic-container
split in `targets/target-c/CURRENT.md`.

Run `python3 tools/check_research_entrypoints.py` before changing active route summaries;
the focused regression tests are `python3 -m unittest tools/test_research_entrypoints.py`.

## Unpromoted working prompts

- [GPT-5.6 Sol xhigh full-settlement run](erdos_problem_99_SOL_XHIGH_FULL_SOLUTION_PROMPT.md)
  is a September 10 working prompt prepared against the older `3f37ef0` checkout.
  It prioritizes the open full-source C-II gate and permits alternate routes or a
  global infinite-family disproof. The accompanying [state review](../reports/repository_state_and_sol_prompt_review_2026-09-10.md)
  explains the frontier and prompt choices. It is preserved for research provenance,
  is not the active whole-problem prompt, and does not promote the named reports.

