## Historical prompts

Other versioned prompts are provenance only unless the state lock explicitly says
otherwise. They record what the research frontier looked like at their own dates. Their
phrases such as “current endpoint,” “next target,” or “remaining gate” are historical
statements.

Do not select a prompt by filename version, modification date, or amount of detail.

## Prompt update rule

Refresh the active route prompt when any of these changes:

- the exact remaining endpoint;
- a major branch is eliminated;
- a regression invalidates a common argument;
- a promoted theorem materially changes the required dependency set.

A frontier-changing promotion must update `../STATE.md`,
`../state/theorem-state.yaml`, the affected route map/current-frontier file, and the
active prompt in the same change.

Use [`PROMPTING_GUIDE.md`](PROMPTING_GUIDE.md) for prompt construction. Do not copy the
entire theorem ledger into a prompt; point to the canonical files and state only the
live endpoint, binding corrections, and output contract.
